      "side": 1,
      "message": "@paligill@gmail.com No concerns from me, as this does not affect the FW update flow.\n\nSeems the change is needed because the registers currently used to calculate the CRC include both non-volatile and volatile registers. The values of the volatile registers can change after an AC cycle, causing the calculated CRC to differ after system resets.\n\nThis change uses only non-volatile registers to calculate the CRC, ensuring that the CRC remains consistent across system resets.",
